 /*
- * ROSEMARY touch bring-up diagnostic (Goodix GT9885 @0x5d or Focaltech @0x38 on
- * MT6785 I2C0). Nothing here is known to work yet: it is a staged probe that logs
- * ("ROSEMARY TOUCH:") what it finds so the next step can be written from facts.
+ * ROSEMARY touch: Focaltech FT3418 (I2C0, 0x38), polled, bit-banged.
  *
- * Boot-arg rosetouch=<mask> (default 1; 0 = off). Stages run in this order:
- *   0x01 read-only dump: infracfg gate registers, GPIO 1/2/51/52, PMIC LDOs, I2C0 regs
- *   0x04 enable MT6359 VIO28 (reg 0x1d5a bit 0) through PWRAP (a guess for "vtp")
- *   0x10 set GPIO51/52 to the SCL0/SDA0 function (mode rosei2cmode, default 1)
- *   0x08 reset pulse: GPIO1 (irq) low, GPIO2 (reset) low 10 ms -> high, then irq input
- *   0x02 I2C0 probe of 0x5d, 0x14 and 0x38 (FIRST I2C0 ACCESS: may hang if its clock is off)
- * rosetouchdelay=<s> (default 45) waits before the stages run.
- * Optional I2C overrides: rosei2ctiming, rosei2cdiv, rosei2cio (written before probing).
+ * Found with the bare-metal stage 10 (shim/rosemary-diag/i2c_diag.c) and the
+ * Android log from TWRP:
+ *   - the touch IC is powered by LDO2 ("vtp", 3.0 V) of the MT6360 sub-PMIC on I2C5
+ *     (GPIO28 = SCL, GPIO29 = SDA, slave 0x64, reg 0x15 = voltage, reg 0x11 bit 6 =
+ *     enable). Its PMIC/LDO blocks drop writes that lack a PEC byte (CRC-8, poly 7,
+ *     over addr_w + reg + value).
+ *   - after the supply is on and GPIO2 (reset) has been pulsed, the FT3418 answers
+ *     on I2C0 (GPIO51 = SCL, GPIO52 = SDA) at 0x38; reg 0xa3 reads 0x54.
+ * Both buses are bit-banged on the GPIO pins: the MediaTek I2C controller was never
+ * made to report NACKs reliably, and a polled bit-bang is plenty for 100 Hz.
+ *
+ * Data layout (FT5x46 family): reg 0 mode, reg 1 gesture, reg 2 low nibble = number of
+ * touches, then 6 bytes per point: [0] event flag (7:6: 0 down, 1 up, 2 contact) and X
+ * high (3:0), [1] X low, [2] id (7:4) and Y high (3:0), [3] Y low, [4] weight, [5] area.
+ * Panel size 1080x2400.
+ *
+ * Boot-args: rosetouch=0 disables; rosetouchdelay=<s> start delay (default 12);
+ * rosetouchlog=<n> log the first n frames (default 12).
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) && defined(ROSEMARY)
